{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2164-11-02 16:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I’ll be taking care of you during your stay. Can you tell me what’s been going on?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2164-11-02 16:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi, Doctor. I’ve been feeling really weak and tired the past couple of days. My husband said I’ve been sleeping a lot more than usual."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2164-11-02 16:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Any nausea or vomiting?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2164-11-02 16:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I’ve had some nausea and threw up once. No fever though."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2164-11-02 16:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see you were recently treated for a UTI with Bactrim. Any symptoms from that now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2164-11-02 16:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No burning or urgency. That seemed to get better, but then I started feeling weak."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2164-11-02 16:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Given your history of Addison’s disease, we’re concerned this could be another adrenal crisis. Your labs show low sodium, high potassium, and your kidney function is down. We gave you IV steroids in the ER."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2164-11-02 16:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, okay. That makes sense. I’ve had this before. Is that why my kidneys are acting up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2164-11-02 16:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, likely due to dehydration from the crisis. We’re giving you IV fluids to help. Your creatinine was 2.3, but it should improve."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2164-11-02 16:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the diarrhea? I’ve had that too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2164-11-02 16:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We tested your stool. No C. diff, salmonella, or shigella. It might be related to your Addison’s flare or the antibiotics. We’ll keep an eye on it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2164-11-02 16:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Should I be worried about my gut issues? I’ve had colitis before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2164-11-02 16:27:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The CT scan showed no signs of colitis or any acute abdominal issue. So that’s reassuring. We think the diarrhea is part of the adrenal crisis this time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2164-11-02 16:28:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, good to know. What about my steroids?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2164-11-02 16:29:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You got 100 mg IV hydrocortisone in the ER. We’ll continue IV steroids today because of the diarrhea—just in case you can’t absorb pills well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2164-11-02 16:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Makes sense. I’ve had trouble with that before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2164-11-03 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your labs are improving. Lactate came down from 3.0 to 2.2, and your kidney function is getting better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2164-11-03 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. I’m feeling a bit stronger today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2164-11-03 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re switching you to oral hydrocortisone now—30 mg in the morning and 15 mg at night—for a few days. Then we’ll taper down as planned with your endocrinologist."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2164-11-03 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I need to stay on this higher dose long?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2164-11-03 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just until your follow-up. Your endocrinologist wants you on 20 mg in the morning and 10 mg at night for now, then adjust from there."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2164-11-03 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I have that appointment next week."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2164-11-03 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your diarrhea has improved, and you’ve tolerated a low-residue diet. That’s a good sign."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2164-11-03 14:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, no episodes today. I think it’s settling down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2164-11-03 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great. We’ll keep you on the current steroid dose and monitor your labs tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2164-11-04 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Morning. Your creatinine is now 0.9, sodium is 140, and bicarbonate is 22. Your kidney function and electrolytes are back to normal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2164-11-04 08:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. Does that mean I can go home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2164-11-04 08:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re planning for discharge tomorrow. You’re stable, afebrile, and tolerating food well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2164-11-04 08:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about my other meds? Anything changed?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2164-11-04 08:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just your hydrocortisone. You’ll take 20 mg in the morning and 10 mg at night. All your other meds—levothyroxine, fludrocortisone, pantoprazole—are the same."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2164-11-04 08:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the citalopram? I saw it was increased."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2164-11-04 08:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, from 10 to 20 mg daily. Your primary doctor thought it might help with your anxiety and low mood, which can flare during illness."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2164-11-04 08:37:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll watch how I feel on it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2164-11-04 13:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re finalizing your discharge plan. You’ll go home tomorrow morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2164-11-04 13:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. Any warning signs I should watch for?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2164-11-04 13:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. If you develop high fever, severe abdominal pain, persistent vomiting, or worsening weakness, come back or call your doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2164-11-04 13:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And if I feel another crisis coming on?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2164-11-04 13:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. If you feel dizzy, nauseated, or extremely weak, especially with low blood pressure, take extra hydrocortisone as directed and seek help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2164-11-05 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "All set for discharge. Your condition is stable, and labs are much improved."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2164-11-05 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor. I feel much better than when I came in."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2164-11-05 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Keep your endocrinology appointment next week. Call if anything changes before then."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2164-11-05 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks again for taking care of me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2164-11-05 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care. We’ll see you at follow-up if needed, but hopefully not before then!"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2164-11-05 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I hope so too!"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2164-11-05 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Nurse will go over your discharge instructions and medications one more time before you leave."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2164-11-05 09:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, sounds good."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2164-11-05 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well. Just keep up with your follow-ups, especially GI, since you’ve had ongoing bowel symptoms."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2164-11-05 09:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I have that scheduled too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2164-11-05 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. Stay hydrated and listen to your body."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2164-11-05 09:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks again."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2164-11-02 16:10:00",
    "admission_end": "2164-11-05 14:21:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient, a woman with a history of Addison’s disease, hypothyroidism, and microscopic colitis, was admitted for weakness, fatigue, nausea, and diarrhea following a recent UTI treated with antibiotics. She presented with tachycardia and lab findings consistent with adrenal crisis, including hyponatremia, hyperkalemia, metabolic acidosis, and acute kidney injury likely due to dehydration. She received IV hydrocortisone in the emergency department and continued IV steroids initially due to concerns about oral absorption from diarrhea. Her symptoms improved, diarrhea resolved, and labs normalized with IV fluids and steroid treatment. She was transitioned to oral hydrocortisone and discharged on a regimen of 20 mg in the morning and 10 mg in the evening to be adjusted at follow-up. Her kidney function recovered, and stool studies were negative for infection. She remained stable, afebrile, and able to tolerate oral intake, and was discharged home with instructions to follow up with endocrinology and GI specialists.",
    "problems": [
      "Glucocorticoid deficiency",
      "Acute kidney failure, unspecified",
      "Urinary tract infection, site not specified",
      "Chronic kidney disease, unspecified",
      "Dehydration",
      "Unspecified acquired hypothyroidism"
    ]
  }
}
